    <fr:title text="Post-Quantum Pressure">Post-Quantum Pressure</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
    Hash-based proof systems are plausibly post-quantum and <fr:link href="/dhsorens-0032/" title="KZG and the Pairing-Based Line" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-0032/" display-uri="dhsorens-0032" type="local">pairing-based</fr:link> ones are not, which turns a cryptographic deadline into an architectural constraint on <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003P/" title="Wrapping and On-Chain Verification" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003P/" display-uri="dhsorens-003P" type="local">wrapping</fr:link>.
</html:p>
    <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>What is at risk and what is not: discrete-log commitments, hash-based commitments, the ROM analysis in a quantum setting.</html:li>
        <html:li>Hash-based signatures and aggregation, and why a SNARK is the aggregation mechanism.</html:li>
        <html:li>Lattice-based commitments as an alternative, and their cost profile.</html:li>
        <html:li>The consequence for the last step of a pipeline that currently ends in Groth16.</html:li>
        <html:li>What VCV-io's lattice work already covers.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
